WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.668 --> 00:00:06.339
MAN: Transylvania, the
name conjures it all--

00:00:06.406 --> 00:00:12.612
dense pine, impassable, craggy
cliffs, thick ground fog.

00:00:12.679 --> 00:00:15.482
This is the mythic forest
of your childhood nightmare.

00:00:18.952 --> 00:00:23.656
Bran Castle, billed as the last
standing relic of a man some

00:00:23.723 --> 00:00:25.291
call Dracula.

00:00:28.128 --> 00:00:31.364
The story goes that Romania's
bottomless well of tyranny,

00:00:31.431 --> 00:00:33.633
catastrophe, and
overall human misery

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:36.936
can all be traced back
to one terrifying ruler

00:00:37.003 --> 00:00:38.671
and his supernatural evil.

00:00:51.918 --> 00:00:53.353
Ah, OK.

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:57.056
So have you ever heard of
the curse of Vlad Tepes?

00:00:57.123 --> 00:00:59.893
Yeah.

00:00:59.959 --> 00:01:00.894
He lost his wife.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:02.195
He lost his dynasty.

00:01:02.262 --> 00:01:03.863
He lost his family.

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:06.266
And he signed a
document in order

00:01:06.332 --> 00:01:10.203
to bring a curse down
against his enemy,

00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:12.472
and he promised
that he will return.

00:01:12.539 --> 00:01:15.742
That was his curse, and I will
take revenge against those

00:01:15.809 --> 00:01:18.578
that they betrayed me.

00:01:18.645 --> 00:01:21.748
He was killed, and his body
was buried in a monastery

00:01:21.815 --> 00:01:23.183
nearby Bucharest.

00:01:23.249 --> 00:01:25.718
Later on when they
opened the coffin,

00:01:25.785 --> 00:01:30.557
they never found his body,
which is quite creepy.

00:01:30.623 --> 00:01:31.858
Yeah, right.

00:01:31.925 --> 00:01:34.694
You do start to wonder what
if he's coming back again?

00:01:34.761 --> 00:01:36.463
So you'd be worried
if you were his enemy.

00:01:36.529 --> 00:01:38.031
You might be a little nervous.
- Oh, yeah.

00:01:38.097 --> 00:01:38.865
Yeah.

00:01:38.932 --> 00:01:41.067
Yeah.

00:01:41.134 --> 00:01:43.069
MAN: Vlad spent much of
his life constructing

00:01:43.136 --> 00:01:45.872
a fearsome persona.

00:01:45.939 --> 00:01:49.776
In some ways, his reputation
was so extreme that it

00:01:49.843 --> 00:01:50.877
haunts the entire world.

00:02:00.553 --> 00:02:01.254
MAN: Gross.

00:02:05.725 --> 00:02:07.093
MAN: Oh my god.

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:08.094
Three days.

00:02:10.864 --> 00:02:12.398
MAN: Yeah.

00:02:12.465 --> 00:02:14.734
What are some of the
other ways he would do it?

00:02:17.804 --> 00:02:18.538
Wow.

00:02:32.685 --> 00:02:34.320
He sounds like
a really nice guy.

00:02:39.125 --> 00:02:41.427
MAN: Yeah, fascists
always say that.

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:47.634
Once he took power
in 1448, Vlad began

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:50.036
a lifelong battle to
protect his country

00:02:50.103 --> 00:02:52.472
from invaders from all sides--

00:02:52.539 --> 00:02:55.441
Hungarians, rival
Nobles, but, most

00:02:55.508 --> 00:02:59.746
of all, the ever expanding
ruthless Ottoman Empire,

00:02:59.812 --> 00:03:02.649
Vlad's mortal enemy.

00:03:02.715 --> 00:03:05.051
The other kings and rulers
of his time had surrendered,

00:03:05.118 --> 00:03:06.653
and they all paid tribute.

00:03:06.719 --> 00:03:12.759
But Vlad fought on with a sheer
hatred that defies description

00:03:12.825 --> 00:03:16.396
perhaps because the Ottomans
had kidnapped him as a child,

00:03:16.462 --> 00:03:19.399
and by the time his father
and brother were killed,

00:03:19.465 --> 00:03:23.336
his hatred had grown so virulent
that we still make TV shows

00:03:23.403 --> 00:03:25.271
about him 600 years later.

00:03:29.576 --> 00:03:32.245
Vlad, himself, he
was right here.

00:03:32.312 --> 00:03:33.346
Yeah, right here.

00:03:35.181 --> 00:03:36.115
MAN: Amazing.

00:03:44.557 --> 00:03:45.291
Wow.

00:03:50.563 --> 00:03:56.202
You know, 600 years ago,
there was a real person here.

00:03:56.269 --> 00:04:02.141
Vlad the Impaler looked
out his little window,

00:04:02.208 --> 00:04:04.444
thought about revenge.

